WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.510
You... you shameless bitch!

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.120
Fukiko-sama!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.600
Fukiko-sama!

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.150
Fukiko-sama!

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:44.990
That song is the one I hate the most in the world!

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.730
Fukiko-sama!

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:55.350
<b>24. Encore</b>

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.360
Why?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.180
Why did she say she hates it?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.760
I knew perfectly well it was her favorite piece.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.160
Why?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.030
Why did she get so upset when I played it?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.990
Nanako! What are you doing?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.860
The 12-minute-after train is coming!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.660
What happened to you this morning?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.460
She hasn't been back since last night.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.660
What? Who? Where?

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.930
If you don't know, don't ask!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.000
OK I won't!

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.610
My Dear Brother...

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.410
I don't understand. Not at all.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.150
About Saint-Juste-sama and Miya-sama.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:15.950
But, though I can't understand the world they share...

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.690
...I know that their kind of world frightens me.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.100
As I see the increasing gloom in Saint-Juste's eyes,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.230
...and the rage hidden behind Miya-sama's kindness,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.100
...I understand their world less and less.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.780
The 25-after bus! The 25-after bus!!

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.380
Darn!

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.850
What'll I do...

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.720
My first-period English teacher, Kusunoki, is very strict!

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:49.790
I'm sorry!

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.000
Rei!

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.000
Hello.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.800
I'm always telling you, don't smoke in this car.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.410
So I do it anyway.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:14.750
Hey, now!

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.350
Can I... play this?

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:20.750
Sure.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.030
That music!

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.500
Are you still upset over yesterday?

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.170
I thought you might know something...

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.180
This violin music...

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:01.590
That piece... once... was one Fukiko practiced very hard on.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.200
I was a freshman then... Six years ago, in the summer.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:08.600
Six years ago?

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.340
I remember that summer very well.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.540
We stayed at the vacation house, near the lake.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.010
Henmi visited us there too.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.880
Henmi Takehiko?

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:25.080
Though he only stayed for one week.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.490
When summer ended,

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.290
...we had a farewell party, inviting the neighbors.

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:36.490
Henmi promised that he'd be back for the party.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.960
He promised.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.770
He said, he'd be back, for sure.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:51.510
That's when Fukiko suddenly started practicing that song.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:58.650
She said she was going to play it at the farewell party.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.900
She practiced hard everyday, sometimes until midnight.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:11.000
She must have really been looking forward to it.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.530
She asked my opinion of it over and over.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:17.200
And?

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.610
At the party, Fukiko did play that violin piece.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.210
And what beautiful playing it was!

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.550
It was had to believe it was being played by a 12 year old.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:31.100
Henmi heard it, too?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.620
No, he never showed up.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:34.690
Oh?

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:38.090
He called right before the party.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.490
He said there was an emergency, and he couldn't come.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:50.640
When she finished playing, the guests applauded with admiration.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.840
They were even asking for an encore.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.380
An encore.

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:02.050
But she didn't respond with an encore.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:10.660
Not only that, but she never played that piece again.

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.190
Never?

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:19.260
In fact I haven't even seen her pick up a violin since then.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:29.410
How did you hear that song, Rei?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.410
I've heard it many times.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.180
When I think back, it was only when she was alone,

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.420
...or no one else was around, that she would play it.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:43.890
I watched from the distance, without being noticed.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.700
I see. That was it.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.430
And then?

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:52.300
Hmm?

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.700
After that, did Henmi visit often?

00:08:56.370 --> 00:09:03.310
No... I'm fairly certain... that was the first and last visit he made.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.310
I see.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:07.580
Could it be...?

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:08.850
Could it be what?

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.380
No. It's nothing.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.660
I'm home.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.530
Welcome back.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.670
Today, I met with Rei.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:29.000
She came to the university to see me.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.140
Any special reason?

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:35.340
No. We just had a talk.

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:37.880
On what subject?

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.950
About 6 years ago, at our vacation home.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.290
Is that so.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.360
And about Henmi.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.770
Oh no!

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:04.170
A single ugly rose has vulgarized this whole arrangement!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.270
That damned girl... this is not her business!

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:44.480
Fukiko-sama, I didn't know.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.080
I honestly didn't know.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:51.890
You were practicing that song just for him.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.490
Just for him, for Henmi Takehiko.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:03.100
You put your heart in it, you put your soul in it,

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:06.100
...but he never came back.

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:08.100
Isn't that right?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:16.510
I didn't know! I really didn't know!

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:33.790
That summer day,

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.800
When I first met him,

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:41.670
Henmi... Takehiko.

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:54.500
Fukiko!

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:55.510
Fukiko!

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:03.960
It's dangerous here! I told you not to come here alone.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.560
I'm sorry, my brother.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:11.300
Let me introduce you to a classmate from school, Henmi Takehiko.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:13.970
This is my sister, Fukiko.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.570
My name is Henmi. Good afternoon.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:19.240
I'll be staying here for a while.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:36.660
That day, everything seemed aglow,

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.730
...as if everything took place in a warm dream.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.690
Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:10.630
No, Thou art more lovely and more temperate.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:20.040
Rough winds do shake the darling buds of May...

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:21.640
Hi!

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.440
This is a book of Shakespeare's poems.

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:27.180
Shakespeare?

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:30.780
Yes, I have to write a report.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.780
Please, read some.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:33.720
What?

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:36.720
Please read something to me.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:40.790
...the poem that you like the best.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:49.200
Rough winds do shake the darling buds of May,

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.400
And summer's lease...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.540
...hath all too short a date.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.620
This is no use... it's just as bad as outside.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.220
Once more...

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:14.360
What?

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:18.830
Please read that poem once more.

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:24.430
Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:28.240
No, Thou art more lovely and more temperate.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:32.440
Rough winds do shake the darling buds of May,

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.780
And summer's lease hath all too short a date,

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:38.050
Sometime too hot the eye of heaven shines,

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.320
and often is his gold complexion dimm'd,

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.190
And every fair from fair sometime declines,

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.590
By chance, or nature's changing course, untrimm'd,

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.390
But the eternal summer shall not fade,

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.590
Not lose possession of that beauty thou possessest,

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:56.930
Nor shall Death brag thou wander'st in his shade,

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.670
When in eternal lines to time thou growest

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:09.150
I love this poem as well!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.420
I love it!

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:18.150
The book is yours, then.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.090
I have another copy.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.160
Is it true what I heard?

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:30.170
You're really leaving tomorrow?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:34.700
Yes. But I promise I'll be back for the party.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.110
Can you promise me that?

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:38.910
Of course!

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:40.780
Then...

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.710
Okay, all right.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:57.530
That summer's day.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:04.070
The sweetest, brightest day of my whole life.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.140
I was so happy then.

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:42.840
Saint-Juste-sama?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.540
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.090
This is the song!

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:38.900
The same song!

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.800
Do you come here often?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:13.530
Wh... what?

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:17.000
Do you come here very often?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:21.470
Well I... I did when Saint-Juste-sama caught a cold...

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:23.410
...several times, actually...

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:25.420
But since then, I haven't... <i> </i>

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:26.970
But since then, I haven't... I warned you back then...

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:31.350
Back then... didn't I warn you? To not get involved with her?

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.620
Y... yes!

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:36.920
My Dear Brother,

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:39.220
What was that all about?

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:43.630
Why did Miya-sama become so upset?

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:49.170
Just being in her room isn't reason enough.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.240
That song... it must somehow be the song...

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:10.260
I was only 12. But my heart died on that summer's day.

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:15.590
We have so many guests here tonight!

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:20.130
Especially since you're going to play the violin...

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:23.070
...twice as many people came this year!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:26.070
My red shoes! Tonight I need my red shoes!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:27.270
Yes, right away!

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:36.950
Brother!

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.890
Does this look good? Red shoes?

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:44.760
Yes! Looks great. Are they new?

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:47.530
Yes. I got them especially for tonight!

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:51.230
One moment, Fukuko... There was a phone call.

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:56.030
That just can't be true, brother.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:59.300
He had some kind of emergency.

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:02.910
Until this morning, he was planning to come.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:06.910
But... he made a promise to me!!

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:09.060
Come on, everyone is waiting.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.250
Show them all the results of all your practicing.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:17.190
After tonight, I'll be known as the brother of a violin prodigy!

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:47.690
So I played on in desperation...

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:51.360
With a pleasant smile, even...

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:56.110
...despite the thorns that were piercing my heart.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:02.030
That summer night's party, in my 12th year...

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:05.370
...my first and last happiness died forever.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:09.190
That was magnificent, Miss Fukiko!

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:18.180
Where are you going!?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:22.990
Don't follow me! I won't forgive you if you follow me!

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:45.140
Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:52.420
No, Thou art more lovely and more temperate.

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:57.020
But thy eternal summer shall not fade,

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:01.430
Nor shall Death brag thou wander'st in his shade,

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:08.100
In eternal lines to time thou growest.

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:24.420
In eternal lines to time thou growest.

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:44.940
No!

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:10.760
That sweetest day, that summers day,

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:13.570
...even if I was betrayed,

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:20.110
...it is mine, forever mine, and mine alone,

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:27.180
...until the day that he returns with me to that summer's day.

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:31.120
I won't allow anyone else to have him.

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:34.120
No matter who it is.

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:40.060
No matter who!

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:05.200
PREVIEW

00:25:05.610 --> 00:25:08.750
Fukiko suddenly summons Nanako to the Sorority House.

00:25:09.020 --> 00:25:12.180
She approaches, drawing her lips close to Nanako's ears...

00:25:12.630 --> 00:25:19.000
...when Rei suddenly rushes in, and reveals a secret,

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:21.700
...which gives Nanako the shock of her life.

00:25:22.160 --> 00:25:23.500
Next episode: <i> </i>

00:25:23.500 --> 00:25:24.830
Next episode: <b>Crimson Lipstick</b>

00:25:25.100 --> 00:25:26.650
Brother, Dear Brother... <i> </i>

00:25:26.650 --> 00:25:29.380
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
